\u2192 contradiction.\\n\\nAh! Important: When you perform \\\"Chi T6\\\", you add the discarded T6 to your hand to complete [T5,T6,T7]. So original hand must have had T5 and T7 (or T5,T6 or T6,T7). After forming the chow, those three tiles are now exposed. So current hand cannot contain T6 or T7 unless duplicate. But T7 has 0 unshown \\u2014 all four copies accounted for: 1 in my chow, others discarded or played. Similarly T6: 3 unshown originally, likely all visible.\\n\\nCross-check discards:\\n- Opposite player played T1, T3, T8, etc.\\n- Next player played T3, T1\\n- Previous player played T6\\n\\nAlso, I played T9 earlier.\\n\\nGiven T7 count is 0 unshown \\u2192 all four are out \\u2192 my meld uses one \\u2192 so other three T7s are discarded \\u2192 safe to assume T7 not in hand now.\\n\\nLikewise T6: started with 4, unshown now 3 \\u2192 one used by me \\u2192 three left unseen \\u2192 possible.\\n\\nBut since I formed [T5,T6,T7] via Chi, I added the discarded T6 to complete it \\u2192 so I contributed T5 and T7 from hand. Then T6 is now in meld. So current hand should NOT include T6 or T7.\\n\\nBut hand says: [T1:1, T2:1, T3:1, T6:1, T7:1] \\u2192 inconsistency.\\n\\nPossibility: typo or misunderstanding. More plausible: the system lists post-meld hand including tiles not used. But logically, after Chi, I discard one tile per turn.\\n\\nReview game history: Last action was \\\"Peng B1\\\", then prior \\\"Play B8\\\", before that \\\"Chi T6\\\", then various plays.\\n\\nSequence likely:\\n- Chi T6 \\u2192 formed [T5,T6,T7]\\n- Then I discarded a tile (e.g., B8)\\n- Now current hand is T1, T2, T3, and maybe extra T6? Unlikely.\\n\\nAlternative: perhaps \\\"T6\\\" in hand is a mistake. Or I have a second T6?\\n\\nBut T6 unshown: 3 remaining \\u2192 total 4 copies. If I used one in chow, 3 elsewhere. Others haven\\u2019t shown T6 except possibly previous player played T6 \\u2192 yes: \\\"Play T6\\\" in previous player\\u2019s history.\\n\\nSo at least one T6 